{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788306397,"nonce":"jrngFoa+a09+4TC14aPir8Dc+rs=","title":"No observer reads Pawn_RecordsTracker: PlantsHarvested, MealsCooked, ThingsConstructed are the direct proof of production, and M1 grades them by inference","message":"Found while rewriting `664e9b9` (the M1 re-run: 20 days, thrive). Its \"real food cycle\" bullet has to prove grow -\u003e harvest -\u003e cook -\u003e eat, and today every proof is an INFERENCE: `zones` growth reaching harvest, a raw-crop def appearing in `things {category:\"food\"}` with no `trade-confirm` row for it, a meal def count rising beside a live `bills` row. Each has a hole — a hunt also raises `food_nutrition`, a caravan sells rice, a meal can be looted off a raider.\n\n**The game keeps the direct answer and no observer reads it.** `RimWorld/Pawn_RecordsTracker` holds per-pawn counters — `RimWorld/RecordDefOf` names `PlantsSown`, `PlantsHarvested`, `MealsCooked`, `ThingsConstructed`, `ThingsCrafted`, `ThingsHauled`, `CellsMined`, `ResearchPointsResearched`, `Kills`, `ShotsFired`, `DamageTaken`, `TimesTendedOther`, `NutritionEaten`, `AnimalsSlaughtered`, `PeopleCaptured`, `PrisonersRecruited` and more (the `[DefOf]` class is the whole list; enumerate `DefDatabase\u003cRecordDef\u003e`, never a hand list). `grep -rn \"records\\|RecordDef\" Source/AutoRimmer/*.cs` returns no reader — the hits are `HistoryAutoRecorder` and comments.\n\n**Why it is worth a verb and a sample column.** Cumulative counters are production RATES once sampled: `plants_harvested` and `meals_cooked` per day are the food cycle as a number, and `things_constructed` per day is \"the colony is building\" without parsing a journal. `2d9a1da`'s append-never-rename column contract is what makes adding them late safe.\n\n**Hazard check the implementer does first.** `Pawn_RecordsTracker.GetValue`/`GetAsInt` read a `DefMap\u003cRecordDef, float\u003e` by index; confirm no accessor on the read path increments or lazily initialises (the `RecordsTick` time counters write on TICK, not on read). Cite the members in `PawnSafe.cs` with the audit.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `records` verb: a free-colonist ROLLUP (sum per RecordDef) plus per-pawn rows capped with `more`; values published with the def's `RecordType` (`Int`/`Time`/`Float`) so a time counter is never read as a count.\n- `pawn {sections:[\"records\"]}` — opt-in, so the 13-section budget is not paid by default.\n- `ColonySampler.Fields` rows for at least `plants_harvested`, `meals_cooked`, `things_constructed` (cumulative), so `trends` carries the per-day rates.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `records` enumerates every `RecordDef` the game has (DefDatabase, not a list), rollup plus capped per-pawn rows, each value typed.\n- Observers never mutate: a save-diff around 20 `records` reads is byte-identical (2.4's method), and the accessors are named in `PawnSafe.cs`.\n- Bench: a rice zone is sown and harvested under `advance`; `PlantsHarvested` moves from 0 and agrees with an independent `things` read of the raw crop; one meal cooked at a stove with a bill moves `MealsCooked` by exactly 1.\n- The three sampler columns land additively; the durable file's header row grows by exactly those names; `trends` publishes their `*_per_day`.\n- Cheap on session 19's axis (field reads over the roster) — measured and stated, not assumed.\n- `664e9b9`'s food-cycle row names this read as its direct proof once it ships; until then the three inferential reads stand.","files":null}]}